WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.250
Ever wondered why lemons are sour or soap

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.329
feels slippery?

00:00:04.329 --> 00:00:05.624
It's all about pH!

00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:08.574
The pH scale measures how acidic or basic

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:09.581
a solution is.

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:11.380
Let's learn how it works.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:16.124
The pH scale usually runs from 0 to 14.

00:00:16.124 --> 00:00:18.918
A pH of exactly 7 is neutral.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:22.000
Pure water is a perfect example,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.987
being neither acidic nor basic.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.283
A solution with a pH below 7 is acidic.

00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.051
The lower the number,

00:00:31.051 --> 00:00:32.903
the stronger the acid.

00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:36.354
Lemon juice and vinegar are common acidic

00:00:36.354 --> 00:00:37.280
substances.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:41.264
A solution with a pH above 7 is basic,

00:00:41.264 --> 00:00:43.079
also known as alkaline.

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:44.814
The higher the number,

00:00:44.814 --> 00:00:46.550
the stronger the base.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.627
Hand soap and baking soda are examples.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.612
pH measures the concentration of hydrogen

00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:57.232
ions, or H+, in a solution.

00:00:57.232 --> 00:00:59.754
More H+ means more acidic,

00:00:59.754 --> 00:01:02.859
while fewer H+ means more basic.

00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:05.673
This determines the pH value.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.942
The pH scale is logarithmic.

00:01:08.942 --> 00:01:11.949
Each step of one pH unit is a tenfold

00:01:11.949 --> 00:01:14.957
change in hydrogen ion concentration.

00:01:14.957 --> 00:01:18.045
A solution with pH 3 is ten times more

00:01:18.045 --> 00:01:19.427
acidic than pH 4!

00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:23.467
The pH scale helps us understand how

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:26.080
acidic or basic substances are.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.271
It measures hydrogen ions,

00:01:28.271 --> 00:01:29.788
runs from 0 to 14,

00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:32.653
and each unit is a tenfold change.
